    "story_origin": {
      "type": "btg-about-origin",
      "settings": {
        "label": "Where It Started",
        "pull_quote": "You can walk a hundred golf courses and never see the people who made them playable.",
        "body": "<p>Every round starts hours before the first tee time. Crews are out before sunrise mowing lines, rolling greens, cutting cups and fixing what yesterday left behind. Most golfers never see any of it.</p><p>Behind The Greens started by pointing the camera the other way: at the superintendents, the crews and the craft that make a course playable. Those stories found an audience fast. Golfers, course professionals and people across the industry recognized the work, and kept coming back for more of it.</p><p>The apparel grew out of that community. Gear made in the same spirit as the stories, for the people who show up before the flag does.</p>",
        "only_on_page": "our-story"
      }
    },
